From 93740085e76599fc2596343bb27fef3a824cb7e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:00:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Long names: drawn tighter, never narrowed; a name that fits
 is drawn as the original drew it

0086/0088 narrowed a long name by scaling the textured quad, which dropped glyph columns (the K of
HerculesKabuterimon read as "<"), and the registration screens moved the Digimon column left and drew boxes past
the title box. drawGlyph places glyphs on its 4-pixel grid; drawStringMode composes a line in software instead
(FIT_STRIP, one upload), each glyph by its ink: FIT_TIGHT the same glyphs with 1 blank column between letters,
FIT_CONDENSED with a 5-column lowercase (font_condensed.h from tools/font/condensed.txt). fitStringMode picks the
first of vanilla / tight / condensed that fits a field.
- Status screen (120 px) and the chart's detail (the original 120 px, centred as the original; a longer name up to
  136 px, centred in the panel): a name that fits is drawn and copied as the original did.
- Battle registration: the box widens to the title box's width only for a name that would pass it (up to 124 px, 12 px inside its edge).
- Registered list: with a name that would pass the cursor (decided over the 40 slots) the list moves under the
  title box, as wide, its cursor too (up to 116 px).
- Save slots and the slot confirmation (the original copied 96 px: "MetalGreymo"): with such a name on the card
  every box and cursor 0x18 further left and 0x110 wide (up to 136 px). The save title holds 17 characters of the
  name; the rest goes to the header's reserved bytes after "LN" and the slot list joins it back.
- Tournament "dealt damage" window (STD): a name past its 120 px tighter, centred by its width.
renderStringFit (utils2.c) and modNameColumn are gone.
